  "description": "18/09/2026, Dean's cost ladder read literally: a Tier N building costs N cards of its own crop. Tier 3 goes from 3 own + 1 any to 3 own + 0 any - one card CHEAPER but no easier to afford, because the binding requirement (three cards of one crop out of a 3.2-card hand) is untouched. This is the control that separates COUNT from CROP: paired against tier3-two-crop-v1, which holds the count and cuts the crop requirement instead. If this arm moves little and that one moves a lot, the ladder's arithmetic is fine and the own-crop tax is the whole fault.",
